# The files that go into the Cornerstone API image. The build context is the repo root, so the list starts empty.
# The image keeps the workspace files, the lock file, the pyproject of the pipeline, the league, facts, analyzer, and
# eggs packages, the API, the deploy script, the values of each client, and the tracked data of each client and the NFL.
# The published pages and the assets of each client are for the site, so the image leaves them out.
# The one exception is the published rankings of each season. The team facts of the analyzer read the playoff odds
# from them, so without them every team fact on Fly says that no odds are on file. Each push to main, the weekly
# publish too, runs Check and then redeploys the API, so the odds in the image stay fresh.
# The last matching line wins, so the line with "!" after the exclusion of the published folder puts the file back.
# Docker reads this file because it sits beside apps/api/Dockerfile.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!apps/pipeline/pyproject.toml
!apps/pipeline/README.md
!packages/league/python/pyproject.toml
!packages/league/python/src
!packages/facts/python/pyproject.toml
!packages/facts/python/src
!packages/analyzer/python/pyproject.toml
!packages/analyzer/python/src
!packages/eggs/python/pyproject.toml
!packages/eggs/python/src
!clients
!data/nfl
!apps/api/pyproject.toml
!apps/api/src
!apps/api/deploy
data/nfl/cache
clients/*/published
!clients/*/published/*/rankings.json
clients/*/assets
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
